---
/**
 * 404.html — GitHub Pages serves this for any URL that has no file.
 *
 * WHY IT EXISTS
 *
 * Without it, Pages serves its own grey "Page not found" document: no navigation, no
 * route back to the site, and a CSP that blocks even the site's stylesheet. That is the
 * experience of every stale link this site has ever produced, and it produces a lot of
 * them — 8 URLs moved in one commit. A visitor arriving from a search result or a
 * pasted link was stranded at a dead end with no way to discover that the page moved
 * rather than disappeared.
 *
 * It cannot fix the underlying problem. Nothing here tells a visitor that /builtins/ is
 * now /docs/builtins/ — that would require a redirect per moved path, which was
 * considered and declined. What it does is keep the site reachable: the sidebar renders
 * normally, so the destination is usually one click away.
 *
 * WHY A ROUTE AND NOT A CONTENT FILE
 *
 * The file must be exactly dist/404.html, at the published root. A content file's URL is
 * derived from its slug, so src/content/pages/404.md would emit /404/ — a real page at
 * the wrong path and still no 404 handler. A route gives the filename directly.
 *
 * Note what this means for the checker: 404.html is not a page in the sidebar and is not
 * in the sitemap, so check.js counts HTML files including it while search.json has one
 * fewer entry. See check.js's page-count assertion.
 */
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { allTitles, LABELS, PAGES, UNLINKED_PAGES, urlFor } from "../nav";
---

<Page
  title="Not found"
  description="That page does not exist. Several documentation pages moved under /docs/; the sidebar lists everything that is here."
  slug=""
  url="/404.html"
  titles={allTitles([])}
  toc={false}
>
  <h1>Not found</h1>

  <p>
    Nothing lives at that URL. Several documentation pages moved under
    <code>/docs/</code>, so a link from before that change lands here — the content is
    not gone, it is in the list on the left.
  </p>

  <p>
    Everything the site publishes:
  </p>

  <!-- Derived from PAGES plus the off-sidebar pages, rather than typed out. A
     hand-written copy would not fail anything when a page moved; it would keep pointing
     at the URL that now 404s, which is the failure this page exists to soften. The
     UNLINKED_PAGES entries are included because they are exactly the pages a visitor
     here may be looking for: /ucks/ changed meaning in the same release that moved eight
     other URLs, and it is not in the sidebar to fall back on. -->
  <ul>
    {[...PAGES.flatMap((s) => s.items), ...UNLINKED_PAGES.map((p) => p.slug)].map(
      (slug) => (
        <li>
          <a href={urlFor(slug)}>{LABELS[slug] ?? slug}</a>
        </li>
      ),
    )}
  </ul>

  <p>
    Source: <a href="https://github.com/fclidev/fcli">github.com/fclidev/fcli</a>
  </p>
</Page>
